 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the environmental conservation law, in relation to extending\nthe authority of the department of environmental conservation to adopt\nregulations for hunting in the northern zone",
    "basePrintNo": "S9316",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S9316-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §11-0907, En Con L",
    "lawSection": "Environmental Conservation Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9316\n\nSPONSOR: MANNION\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the environmental conservation law, in relation to\nextending the authority of the department of environmental conservation\nto adopt regulations for hunting in the northern zone\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of this bill amends ECL § 11-0907(8Xc) to extend, until Decem-\nber 31, 2027, DEC's authority to establish a special deer hunting season\nin the Northern Zone for muzzle-loading firearms.\n\nSection 2 of this bill provides that the bill shall take effect imme-\ndiately.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nAuthority to set regulations provides a timely administrative process\nwhich optimizes the effectiveness of harvest management techniques.\nThis legislation would extend DEC's authority to set by regulation the\nlength and timing of the early and late Northern Zone muzzle-loading\nseasons, and to specify the taking of deer of either sex, antlerless\ndeer only, legal bucks only, or any combination thereof. This flexibili-\nty allows DEC to set muzzle-loading seasons to promote recreational\nhunting and herd control most effectively.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis authority was last extended by Chapter 205 of the Laws of 2021.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nSection 2 of this bill provides that the bill shall take effect imme-\ndiately.\n",
